      "text": "# Transactional Inventory Ledger: Design & Reference Implementation\n\n## 1. Design Overview\n\nThis system implements an **append-only, double-entry-style inventory ledger** in SQLite with:\n- **Idempotent transactions** via client-generated UUIDs\n- **Optimistic concurrency control** with versioned stock levels\n- **Audit invariants** enforced at the database level\n- **Safe migrations** with rollback support\n- **Full test coverage**\n\n### Core Principles\n1. **Immutability**: Stock movements are never updated/deleted; corrections are new entries.\n2. **Idempotency**: Re-submitting the same transaction ID is a no-op.\n3. **Consistency**: Stock levels are derived from the ledger, never stored as mutable truth.\n4. **Auditability**: Every change is traceable to a transaction with timestamp, actor, and reason.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Schema Design\n\n```sql\n-- ============================================================\n-- INVENTORY LEDGER SCHEMA\n-- ============================================================\n\n-- Products: static catalog (not part of ledger)\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS products (\n    product_id   TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n    name         TEXT NOT NULL,\n    sku          TEXT UNIQUE NOT NULL,\n    created_at   TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT (strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%fZ', 'now')),\n    updated_at   TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT (strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%fZ', 'now'))\n);\n\n-- Stock movements: the immutable ledger\n-- Each row represents a single atomic change to a product's stock.\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS stock_movements (\n    movement_id      INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,\n    transaction_id   TEXT NOT NULL,          -- Client-generated UUID for idempotency\n    product_id       TEXT NOT NULL,\n    quantity_change  INTEGER NOT NULL,       -- Positive = inbound, Negative = outbound\n    balance_after    INTEGER NOT NULL,       -- Stock level after this movement (denormalized for audit)\n    movement_type    TEXT NOT NULL CHECK (movement_type IN ('INBOUND', 'OUTBOUND', 'ADJUSTMENT', 'TRANSFER_IN', 'TRANSFER_OUT')),\n    reason           TEXT,                   -- Human-readable reason\n    actor            TEXT NOT NULL,          -- User/system that initiated the movement\n    created_at       TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT (strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%fZ', 'now')),\n    FOREIGN KEY (product_id) REFERENCES products(product_id)\n);\n\n-- Indexes for performance\nCREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_movements_transaction_id ON stock_movements(transaction_id);\nCREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_movements_product_id ON stock_movements(product_id);\nCREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_movements_created_at ON stock_movements(created_at);\n\n-- Unique constraint: one movement per transaction_id per product\n-- This enforces idempotency at the DB level\nCREATE UNIQUE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_movements_txn_product ON stock_movements(transaction_id, product_id);\n\n-- View: current stock levels derived from ledger\nCREATE VIEW IF NOT EXISTS current_stock AS\nSELECT\n    p.product_id,\n    p.name,\n    p.sku,\n    COALESCE(SUM(sm.quantity_change), 0) AS current_stock,\n    MAX(sm.created_at) AS last_movement_at\nFROM products p\nLEFT JOIN stock_movements sm ON p.product_id = sm.product_id\nGROUP BY p.product_id, p.name, p.sku;\n\n-- View: audit trail with running balance verification\nCREATE VIEW IF NOT EXISTS audit_trail AS\nSELECT\n    sm.movement_id,\n    sm.transaction_id,\n    sm.product_id,\n    p.sku,\n    sm.quantity_change,\n    sm.balance_after,\n    sm.movement_type,\n    sm.reason,\n    sm.actor,\n    sm.created_at,\n    -- Verify balance_after matches running sum\n    (\n        SELECT COALESCE(SUM(sm2.quantity_change), 0)\n        FROM stock_movements sm2\n        WHERE sm2.product_id = sm.product_id\n          AND sm2.movement_id <= sm.movement_id\n    ) AS computed_balance,\n    CASE\n        WHEN sm.balance_after = (\n            SELECT COALESCE(SUM(sm2.quantity_change), 0)\n            FROM stock_movements sm2\n            WHERE sm2.product_id = sm.product_id\n              AND sm2.movement_id <= sm.movement_id\n        ) THEN 'VALID'\n        ELSE 'INVALID'\n    END AS balance_check\nFROM stock_movements sm\nJOIN products p ON sm.product_id = p.product_id;\n```\n\n### Key Design Decisions\n\n| Aspect | Decision | Rationale |\n|--------|----------|-----------|\n| **Stock storage** | Derived from `SUM(quantity_change)` | Single source of truth",
